WEBVTT

00:00:00.591 --> 00:00:05.951
Meet Suhail Health. A connected workspace
for hospitals, clinics, and organizations

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.921
coordinating screening follow-up.

00:00:08.315 --> 00:00:11.153
An actionable result is the start of a journey.

00:00:11.547 --> 00:00:16.433
Suhail connects explanation, consultation,
referral, and documented care.

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:20.217
Patients see their next step. Teams see who owns the work.

00:00:20.611 --> 00:00:25.340
And with Ask Suhail, each signed-in user
can ask about their own permitted records

00:00:25.655 --> 00:00:27.941
and jump straight to the relevant detail.

00:00:29.311 --> 00:00:33.961
The public page introduces the service,
its audiences, and the connected care

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:38.218
journey. Secure sign-in opens an authorized workspace.

00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:42.868
Separate synthetic demonstration access
lets reviewers explore fictional cases by

00:00:43.025 --> 00:00:47.676
role. Inside, each person sees the work and records permitted to their

00:00:47.912 --> 00:00:48.464
account.

00:00:49.871 --> 00:00:52.866
Switch between the focused list and the journey board.

00:00:53.103 --> 00:00:55.585
Both show the same authorized cases.

00:00:55.861 --> 00:01:00.748
Summary cards filter the real queue,
including urgent review and reconciliation.

00:01:01.142 --> 00:01:05.635
Open an episode to see independent
milestones, current ownership, and the next

00:01:05.713 --> 00:01:10.758
action. Select a milestone to inspect
its recorded state, linked evidence, and

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:15.172
assigned work. The activity record preserves how the case changed.

00:01:16.551 --> 00:01:21.201
On a phone, the patient sees the next step and responsible team first.

00:01:21.438 --> 00:01:25.458
Receiving an update and understanding it are separate actions.

00:01:25.655 --> 00:01:30.187
Patients can ask a clinician a question,
request practical support, or provide

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:32.630
appointment preferences for staff confirmation.

00:01:33.103 --> 00:01:36.571
Ask Suhail helps locate their own plan and care team.

00:01:36.965 --> 00:01:41.063
English and right-to-left Arabic support
the patient journey, with section

00:01:41.142 --> 00:01:43.901
navigation that follows the visible content.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:50.079
The clinical workspace brings assigned
episodes and unanswered questions together.

00:01:50.315 --> 00:01:54.414
A human reply records the response, agreed action, and owner.

00:01:54.808 --> 00:01:57.488
Clinicians can request a specialist opinion;

00:01:57.567 --> 00:02:00.325
specialists see their assigned consultations.

00:02:00.562 --> 00:02:04.345
Optional AI assistance prepares source-linked drafts for review.

00:02:04.739 --> 00:02:09.626
A draft stays separate from a human
consultation, verified evidence, and a clinical

00:02:09.705 --> 00:02:10.650
disposition.

00:02:12.111 --> 00:02:16.998
Receiving services see a minimum referral
packet with its reason, source version,

00:02:17.077 --> 00:02:21.806
and granted scope. Ask Suhail answers
workload questions from that provider’s

00:02:21.885 --> 00:02:24.801
permitted packets and links back to the right referral.

00:02:25.274 --> 00:02:28.663
Explicit acceptance changes the agreed responsibility.

00:02:29.136 --> 00:02:32.958
Rejection preserves its reason and creates recovery work.

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:38.042
Accepted services can report unavailable
capacity, confirm an appointment, and

00:02:38.239 --> 00:02:40.091
record attendance or a no-show.

00:02:40.486 --> 00:02:43.953
A proposed transfer keeps the sending owner accountable.

00:02:45.351 --> 00:02:48.189
Returned evidence starts pending verification.

00:02:48.583 --> 00:02:53.075
An authorized clinician reads the retained
document, inspects provenance, and

00:02:53.154 --> 00:02:55.834
checks the patient, order, and result version.

00:02:56.307 --> 00:02:59.065
The closure checklist shows remaining requirements.

00:02:59.538 --> 00:03:04.583
If onward care is needed, referral
acceptance alone is insufficient: treatment

00:03:04.661 --> 00:03:09.706
initiation or an accepted, owned
surveillance plan must support the endpoint.

00:03:09.942 --> 00:03:14.435
Only an authorized clinical disposition
records completed required care.

00:03:15.791 --> 00:03:19.732
Trusted urgent signals route to staff without waiting for a model.

00:03:20.126 --> 00:03:24.067
Acknowledgement and the clinician’s
disposition are recorded separately.

00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:28.481
Identity conflicts enter quarantine until authorized reconciliation.

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:31.515
Corrected results reopen affected work.

00:03:31.712 --> 00:03:34.195
Earlier evidence is marked superseded.

00:03:34.392 --> 00:03:39.121
Decline, inability to contact, and other
exceptions retain their category and

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.461
residual need.

00:03:41.831 --> 00:03:46.087
The completed patient view displays
the approved care plan, reviewed source

00:03:46.166 --> 00:03:48.294
evidence, and the responsible team.

00:03:48.846 --> 00:03:53.023
Earlier communication and understanding remain historical records.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:55.782
Questions and requests for help stay available.

00:03:56.255 --> 00:04:00.590
The wording follows the documented
outcome, keeping the next step readable and

00:04:00.669 --> 00:04:02.324
connected to its source.

00:04:03.711 --> 00:04:08.204
Operations measures independent milestones
against the full actionable-episode

00:04:08.283 --> 00:04:13.485
denominator. Completed care, open
episodes, and documented exceptions stay

00:04:13.563 --> 00:04:18.450
distinct. Delivery records show integration
status, attempts, and links to the

00:04:18.529 --> 00:04:23.810
underlying case. Urgent acknowledgements
link back to their cases, and overdue work

00:04:23.888 --> 00:04:28.302
has its own queue. The dashboard makes
unfinished work visible, with clear

00:04:28.381 --> 00:04:30.746
definitions and traceable records.

00:04:32.151 --> 00:04:37.117
Software verification includes fifteen
hundred passing deterministic checks.

00:04:37.353 --> 00:04:42.003
Execution records preserve the source,
model configuration, and spending controls

00:04:42.082 --> 00:04:47.048
behind each measurement. Suhail Health
connects patients and care teams across the

00:04:47.127 --> 00:04:51.461
screening-to-care journey. Six focused agents support the workflow.

00:04:51.934 --> 00:04:55.205
Ask Suhail brings permitted context within reach.

00:04:55.402 --> 00:04:57.530
The care team stays in control.

